# Java / Spring Boot

## Structure

- `@RestController` → `@Service` → `@Repository` → JPA entity
- Validate requests with `@Valid`; document APIs with Springdoc OpenAPI
- Global errors via `@ControllerAdvice` delegating to `TmsException`

## Naming

- Classes: PascalCase | Methods/fields: camelCase | Constants: ALL_CAPS

## Patterns

```java
// ✅ Domain error
throw new TmsException(ErrorCode.TICKET_NOT_FOUND);

// ✅ Constructor injection
public TicketService(TicketRepository repo) { this.repo = repo; }

// ❌ Business logic in controller
@GetMapping("/{id}")
public Ticket get(@PathVariable Long id) {
    return repo.findById(id).orElseThrow(...); // belongs in service
}
```

## Java 21

Use records for DTOs, sealed classes for closed hierarchies, pattern matching where it aids clarity.

## Data & Performance

- Spring Data JPA with Flyway/Liquibase migrations
- Index frequently queried columns; return empty collections not null
- `@Async` and Spring Cache only when justified

## Testing

JUnit 5 + Spring Boot Test: unit tests, MockMvc (web), `@DataJpaTest` (repos), `@SpringBootTest` (integration).
